  "audit_assessment": {
    "score": 0,
    "reason": "The agent produced and executed a two-panel PNG with two highlighted intervals per experiment, but it does not compute or visualize the requested optimal two-peak segmentation model. The reference constructs both per-base and read-end coverage tracks and applies PeakSegDisk sequentialSearch_dir(..., 2L), plotting fitted piecewise-constant model segments and change boundaries. In contrast, the agent bins reads into 1-kb bins, finds a least-squares three-segment partition, then zeros its middle segment and repeats the same procedure to create a second interval. That heuristic is not a joint optimum for a two-peak segmentation model. Its rendered output only recolors raw binned traces in the selected intervals; it omits fitted segment means and boundary/model-step presentation. The different intervals and scales therefore reflect a materially different, unsupported calculation rather than an acceptable alternative implementation of the specified model.",
    "reference_method": "The reference converts reads into two coverage representations (bases counted at every covered base and at read ends), runs PeakSegDisk::sequentialSearch_dir(data.dir, 2L) independently for each representation and experiment, then plots exact coverage plus the fitted model's horizontal segment means and vertical change boundaries in a bases.counted-by-experiment facet grid.",
    "agent_method": "The agent creates separate 1-kb binned count tracks, exhaustively minimizes within-segment squared error for a three-segment partition, treats the middle segment as one peak, zeros that interval, and repeats to derive another non-overlapping interval. The plot overlays red/blue raw binned signal for those intervals on a gray raw trace; it does not draw a fitted segmentation model.",
    "file_observations": [
      {
        "file": "segmentation_model_plot.png",
        "assessment": "different",
        "reason": "The reference image has four facets (each/end coverage for both experiments) with black exact signal and cyan fitted model steps/boundaries. The agent image has only two stacked experiment panels and gray/red/blue binned raw traces. Although both have genomic position and signal axes and label two intervals, the agent does not display fitted piecewise-constant segmentation levels or model change boundaries, and its signal scales/intervals materially differ.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "A-0006",
          "A-0007",
          "A-0001",
          "A-0003"
        ]
      }
    ],
